        "mission_intent": "We need to stand up a comprehensive Information Security Continuous Monitoring specification for the enterprise that aligns with our NIST SP 800-137 obligations, and I'd like the draft ready for leadership review by end of next quarter. The spec should begin with a formal ISCM strategy section that explicitly anchors to our documented organizational risk tolerance and demonstrates how it will guide prioritization of monitoring efforts consistently across all three organizational tiers\u2014governance, mission/business process, and information system. Include a metrics framework that provides meaningful indicators of security status at each tier, with defined collection frequencies, data sources such as our Splunk SIEM, Tenable vulnerability scanner feeds, and ServiceNow CMDB, and escalation criteria when metrics deviate from acceptable ranges. The specification must address how we verify the continued effectiveness of all deployed security controls, including automated and procedural controls, and must cover compliance verification against our derived information security requirements from applicable mandates. Ensure the document accounts for the full scope of technology, processes, procedures, operating environments, and people, and define roles and responsibilities for monitoring activities, reporting cadences for each tier, and how findings feed back into risk management decisions when resources are constrained and prioritization is necessary.",
